  type checks (ann, undef, arity, immut, mut, unary, cmp, if/while,
  logic, missing return, refinements)
  then `check_typestate(src, toks)` at line 105
  then more type checks (must-use, call lits, field, struct)

Prior audit said `:98`. Live is `:105`.

`check_typestate.oo:16-21`: parse directives from `src`; if no
`__tsf__` fn, return; else `ts_walk_program`.

Parse (`check_typestate_parse.oo`):
  `// TYPESTATE: Type S1 S2` → machine, states stored as `Type#S`
  `// TYPESTATE fn name: From -> To` and `-> To`
  `// TYPESTATE end S` → `__tsend__Type`
  unknown From/To refused
  two machines must not share a raw state name? Board
  `TYPE_STATE.oot:36` says state names are global and two machines
  must not share a name. Parse keys `__tss__` as `Type#state` so
  `Sock Open` and `File Open` can both exist (`:146`). Board line
  22 agrees. Line 36 conflicts with line 22. Residual docs, not
  a code hole. `typestate_two_types.oo` is a smoke OK case.

Walk:
  paren call and `s.fn()` (`check_typestate_walk.oo:113-134`)
  first arg must be a bare IDENT (`:52-64`); nested call / field
  / index yields empty arg and is refused on From→To
  let/assign alias (`:92-95`, `:143-146`)
  ctor `>To` (`:101-102`)

Fn compose (`check_typestate_fn.oo:134-174`):
  body text that calls another TYPESTATE fn sets `__tscompose__`
  live exit must leave first param as To
  leaf body trusts the directive
  process_exit does not require To (`check_typestate_join.oo:229-235`)
  param rebind refused (`:126-132`)

Join (`check_typestate_join.oo`):
  if/else both sides same state; missing else keeps pre
  return / process_exit mark `__tsdiv__` and do not join
  while/for body must leave pre states unchanged
  transition in if/loop condition refused (`:168-170`, `:215-217`)
  match arms join like if/else (`check_typestate_match.oo:12-45`)

`ts_merge_branch` builds a fresh env of `__tsv__` names from the
pre bag (`:51-95`). `__tsa__` alias links are not copied. Use of
